            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-3",
                    "linecount": 71,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 460.0, 1043.0 ],
                    "text": "BandbAss 0.02 BETA — mrelwood plugins\nPage: https://mrelwood5.wixsite.com/plugins/bandbass\n(Individual page exists; the plugin ships in the free mrelwood_PluginPack.)\n\nWhat it is: a sidechain bass compressor: the LOW band of the main signal\nis compressed through a shelving LP filter whenever a sidechain kick hits,\nwhile the frequencies above the crossover stay untouched. In this RNBO\nport, in1/in2 is the bass, in3 is the kick sidechain, in4 is an optional\nsecond sidechain (channel4/auto detection). NOTE: with NO sidechain input\nthe gain does eventually return to unity - the source does not implement\nthe standalone compressor in its own description (README note). Parameter\nvalues keep the original JSFX slider units.\n\nParameters (original names):\n\n- crossover   (Hz) 100..500, default 200\n  Band split frequency (shelving LP). Internally two LP chains at\n  1.2x and 0.8x of this value. 100-200 Hz snares other bass well;\n  300-500 leaves more mid-bass untouched.\n\n- threshold_kick  (dB) -40..0, default -20\n  Sidechain detector threshold. Full-scale kick = 0 dBFS, so -10..-20 is\n  a typical full-scale level; deeper/darker programs need threshold\n  higher up. Use the 'Link' parameter to make threshold_bass follow this.\n\n- threshold_bass  (dB) -40..0, default -20\n  Threshold for the bass source envelope. Optionally ignored when\n  link_thresholds is engaged (it then rides with threshold_kick).\n\n- attack  (slider units) 0..50, default 0\n  Attack of the duck: NOT milliseconds. Internally\n  attack = sampleRate * (0.5a + 0.5a^2) * 50ms with a = attack/50, so\n  it has its own non-linear taper; 0 = fastest (sample-level), 50 =\n  50 ms slower (smooth pump).\n\n- hold  (slider units) 0..100, default 0\n  Hold before release, same style of non-linear mapping\n  (a = hold/100, up to 100 ms). Longer holds unpump melodic bass\n  tracks with busy kicks.\n\n- release  (slider units) 10..300, default 30\n  Release of the duck, again non-linearly mapped:\n  rel = 5 + (0.25r + 0.75r^2) * 295 ms. Musically: 30-80 for fast\n  kick-following duck, 150-300 for a lazy swelling.\n\n- depth  (%) 0..200, default 100\n  Ducking depth: 100 = gain goes all the way down to the threshold\n  level; above 100 the source allows \"over-compression\" up to 2x\n  (depth2 = max(1, depth/100)) for a nasty, almost kick-gating feel.\n\n- stereo  (enum: 0 = Mono, 1 = Stereo) default 0\n  Default is Mono: the main inputs are averaged; Stereo mode keeps\n  both channels distinct. Even in Stereo the LEFT main envelope is\n  what controls both channels (source behavior).\n\n- channel4  (discrete: -1 = disabled, 0 = auto, +1 = enabled) default 0\n  Whether to pay attention to the optional second sidechain (in4).\n  'Auto' (0) means the source detects it by itself; -1 disables\n  and +1 forces it. Change this value to reset the detection state.\n\n- link_thresholds  (enum: 0 = Separate, 1 = Link) default 1\n  When 'Link', threshold_bass tracks threshold_kick, so you only set\n  one threshold. In the original JSFX this linking exists only as a\n  UI gesture, not in the DSP - the RNBO port implements it here as a\n  real DSP function, so automation works as you'd expect.\n\nMusical notes: for a classic \"bass ducks under kick\" track, set\ncrossover ~150-250 Hz, thresholds around -10 to -20, Hold 0-30,\nRelease 30-80 and Depth 100. The 0.02 BETA warning is real: check\nthe source's silence behavior at very low level and don't rely on it\nas a general compressor without the kick sidechain.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
